    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d379">

                <pb facs="0516" n="412" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg412"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.911/24.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 719.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-06-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 27, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence in
                    regard to the libelous attacks upon Mr. Gibson and myself by the newspaper
                    “Cuba,” and <pb facs="0517" n="413" xml:id="pg413"/> particularly to my telegram
                    of June 16, I have the honor to transmit herewith enclosed copy and translation
                    of an editorial from “Cuba” of the 13th instant, wherein the paper makes
                    retraction of its charges.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. M. Beaupré</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d379-a1.xml" xpointer="d379-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
